<article class="env-corollary" id="0314">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0314">Corollary <span data-tag="0314">7.3.8.14</span>.</a> Let $\overline{F}: \overline{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a functor of $\infty $-categories, and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{0} \subseteq \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\subseteq \overline{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ be full subcategories. Then $\overline{F}$ is left Kan extended from $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^0$ if and only if it satisfies the following pair of conditions: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(1)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The functor $\overline{F}$ is left Kan extended from $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(2)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The restriction $\overline{F}|_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ is left Kan extended from $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{0}$. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Proposition <a data-tag="0312" href="/tag/0312">7.3.8.12</a> in the special case $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}= \Delta ^0$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
